        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ecde66e6-4ae5-5425-a313-c5da89a8f20e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beyazıt Tower, Beyazıt Square, Istanbul, Turkey, Golden Horn, Fatih district\n- Organizations: Istanbul University, Ottoman Ministry of War\n- Systems: Istanbul University Observatory\n- People: Constantine the Great, Mustafa Yektaoğlu\n- Topics: Miniatürk, Istanbul Faculty of Medicine\n\nFacts:\n- Constantine the Great built the city of Istanbul on seven hills following the model of Rome.\n- Beyazıt Square in Istanbul was known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period.\n- Beyazıt Tower, also called Seraskier Tower after the Ottoman Ministry of War, is an 85 m fire-watch tower in the courtyard of Istanbul University’s main campus on Beyazıt Square in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Miniatürk is a miniature park on the north-eastern shore of the Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Istanbul University Observatory was established in 1936 next to Beyazıt Tower within Istanbul University’s main campus at Beyazıt Square in Fatih district, Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Mustafa Yektaoğlu studied at the Istanbul Faculty of Medicine at Istanbul University and graduated in 1978.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1966e04d-346a-5e41-89fd-182876f82885",
        "text": "Page: Beyazıt Tower. Sentence: Beyazıt Tower, also named Seraskier Tower, from the name of the Ottoman ministry of War, is an 85 m tall fire-watch tower located in the courtyard of Istanbul University's main campus (formerly Ottoman Ministry of War) on Beyazıt Square (known as the Forum Tauri in the Roman period) in Istanbul, Turkey, on top of one of the \"seven hills\" which Constantine the Great had built the city, following the model of Rome.\nPage: Miniatürk. Sentence: Miniatürk is a miniature park situated at the north-eastern shore of Golden Horn in Istanbul, Turkey.\nPage: Istanbul University Observatory. Sentence: Established in 1936, it is situated next to the historic Beyazıt Tower within the main campus of the university at Beyazıt Square in Fatih district of Istanbul, Turkey.\nPage: Mustafa Yektaoğlu. Sentence: He studied at the Istanbul Faculty of Medicine at Istanbul University graduating in 1978.",
